  "body": "## Issue\nCloses #763\nRefs #768 (the `<svg>`/`<math>` follow-up of the round-5 review of #771; #768's part 2, the `R267a` prose handle, stays open)\nClaim: cloud/i763-opus\n\n## What and why\n**Problem.** A member's signature is member input. With `… </span>TEXT<span class=\"x\">…` inside it, `anonymize` stopped at the stray `</span>`, so `TEXT` survived, and `check` reported nothing (it only looked inside the span).\n\n**Cause.** `_find_para_blocks` ends a `span.signature` with a depth count of `<span>` tags, which the member's own markup can unbalance. `check` had no rule on what follows a signature.\n\n**Change.**\n- `anonymize`: a signature runs to the last `</span>` before the end of its `div#para…` and of its `td.messCase2`, when that is further than the depth count (`PERSONAL_CONTAINERS`, `_personal_block_end`). HFR's structure: all 336 corpus signatures are the last child of their para div (followed by `</div></td>`). A stray `</div>` is covered by the `td` container.\n- `check` (`StructuralVerifier`, own walk, LESSONS 33-34): no element and no text may follow a signature in its parent; a signature or mood span carries one attribute, `class`, with exactly one token (`signature` or `MoodStatus`), so no duplicate or extra class; any `<svg>` or `<math>` is unexpected markup (html.parser reads `<style>`/`<script>` as raw text where a browser does not, #768).\n- Issue point 2 (`title=`, empty `<a href>`, ``'&lt;img alt/src&gt;'``) was already refused by #771's walk; the new test pins it next to the class rule.\n\n**Why no wider.** The mood status is left to the depth count: in the corpus it is followed by HFR's own markup in its cell (`R63a`, `R33b`), so the signature rule would over-redact. Follow-up: #793.\n\n## How it was verified\nTests first, red before the change (6 failures, `python3 -m unittest tests.test_anonymize`):\n- `test_unbalanced_span_end_in_a_signature_does_not_end_the_redaction`: \"Secret Handle\" and \"Other Words\" survived; now gone, separator and clear div kept, `findings` empty.\n- `test_unbalanced_span_and_div_ends_in_a_signature_are_redacted_too`: stray `</span>` and `</div>`.\n- `test_check_refuses_content_after_a_signature_in_its_container`: text, `<img>`, empty `<a>` after the signature fail `check`; HFR's real shape passes, and so does a mood followed by HFR's avatar div.\n- `test_check_refuses_a_member_value_in_a_signature_attribute`: `class=\"signature RealHandle\"` passed before.\n- `test_check_refuses_svg_and_math`: `<svg><style><span class=\"signature\">…` passed before.\n- (A sixth red test, for the mood, was dropped with the mood rule; see #793.)\n\nAfter the change:\n- `python3 -m unittest discover tooling/fixtures/tests`: OK.\n- `python3 tooling/fixtures/anonymize.py check --corpus Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/captures --quiet`: `ok 691 of 691 corpus files clean`.\n- `python3 tooling/fixtures/manifest_check.py`: OK.\n- Old vs new `anonymize` on every HTML page of the corpus (282): identical output, no over-redaction.\n\nLinux-only change (`tooling/fixtures/` only): no macOS job expected.\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected (tooling only)\n- [x] Tests added, seen red first\n- [x] No secrets; invented names only\n- [x] Docs: no protocol change; README rule unchanged (check refuses more)\n- [ ] Author model: Opus / Reviewer model: Fable (pending)\n- [x] No legacy behaviour or gap row: no ledger\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CETDfMpvh9JwfngVyq)_",
